esults, on sites with Woo Discount Rules: a page with a Price filter made the plugin evaluate the discount rules for every product on every view (5–50 seconds on large catalogs); the discounted prices are now cached and recalculated only for the products or rules that changed\n* Fix   - Fixed filtered category pages in a non-default Polylang language (e.g. /uk/product-category/…/) being 301-redirected to the default language as soon as a filter was applied — the plugin copied Polylang&#039;s internal language condition into its own tax query, so Polylang resolved the queried category in the wrong language\n* Fix   - Fixed filters on sites where Polylang uses a separate domain or sub-domain for each language: filter links, chips and the Reset link pointed to the default language&#039;s domain, and AJAX filtering returned «page not found» on the other languages&#039; domains\n* Fix   - Fixed the «What to filter» field of a Filter Set staying empty when the selected page is on another domain than the admin — for example a Filter Set of a language that Polylang serves from its own domain or sub-domain\n* Fix   - Fixed filtering on Divi Theme Builder category archive templates whose Blog module shows the «Current Category» (Divi 4 and Divi 5): the filter widget and its counters reacted, but the Blog module kept listing all posts of the category</p>\";}s:37:\"translatepress-multilingual/index.php\";O:8:\"stdClass\":13:{s:2:\"id\";s:41:\"w.org/plugins/translatepress-multilingual\";s:4:\"slug\";s:27:\"translatepress-multilingual\";s:6:\"plugin\";s:37:\"translatepress-multilingual/index.php\";s:11:\"new_version\";s:5:\"3.3.9\";s:3:\"url\";s:58:\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/translatepress-multilingual/\";s:7:\"package\";s:76:\"https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/translatepress-multilingual.3.3.9.zip\";s:5:\"icons\";a:2:{s:2:\"1x\";s:72:\"https://ps.w.org/translatepress-multilingual/assets/icon.svg?rev=3166541\";s:3:\"svg\";s:72:\"https://ps.w.org/translatepress-multiling